course: dictionary
lesson: 1045
title: Boring: a word with two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Boring» most often describes something that is not interesting. «Nearly everyone finds practice boring sometimes, even professionals.» Even experts can find practice dull, so the writer is saying practice can feel dull, not that it is bad or unkind.
explain: The word also turns up as a verb form: bore, bores, bored, boring. Here boring means making a hole through something with a tool. Check the clues: the words around it, like through wood or rock, tell you which meaning fits.
explain: To choose the right meaning, swap your idea into the sentence. «A fair rule is boring, and it works.» Try "a fair rule is not interesting, and it works": it still makes sense. Try "a fair rule is making a hole, and it works": it does not, so this meaning is wrong here.
fact: «Boring» means not interesting, so you feel tired of it or want something else to do.
fact: Being bored is normal, and it can lead to new ideas and games.
fact: As a verb form, «boring» means making a hole through something with a tool, like boring through wood or rock.
fact: Phrases you may hear: «a boring day», «so boring», «boring old».
fact: In stories, boring places can become exciting when something happens.
exercise: «Nearly everyone finds practice boring sometimes, even professionals.» What does boring mean here? | Brand new and shiny | *Not interesting, so you feel tired of it | Making a hole through wood | Very exciting and loud
exercise: The workers are boring through the rock to make a tunnel. What is boring doing here? | Falling asleep | Telling a joke | *Making a hole through the rock with a tool | Running very fast
exercise: «A fair rule is boring, and it works.» Why might the writer say boring? | It is the most exciting rule ever | *It is plain and ordinary, not exciting, but it works | It has a hole in it
test: «Sam wants chess club, but Jake says chess is "mid", nothing special.» Jake's word mid is like boring. What does boring mean in this sentence? | Very loud | Full of treasure | Making a hole in wood | *Not interesting, nothing special
test: Dad bores holes in the wall for the new shelf. What is Dad doing? | Shouting at the wall | Reading a book about shelves | *Making holes in the wall with a tool | Cooking his dinner
exam: What does «boring» mean when it describes a long wait? | *Not interesting, so you feel tired of it | Very tall | Hungry | Shiny and new
